The fix has been applied and tests pass. Here's a summary:

**Bug:** Line 7 used exact string comparison (`b.url === inc.url`), which is case-sensitive. URLs with different hostname casing (e.g. `https://example.com/a` vs `https://EXAMPLE.com/a`) were treated as different URLs, so the incoming bookmark was appended instead of merged.

**Fix:** Replaced the string comparison with proper URL parsing — both URLs are parsed via `new URL()`, then compared by:
- hostname (case-insensitive via `.toLowerCase()`)
- pathname (exact)
- search/query string (exact)

Invalid/malformed URLs fall back to the original exact string comparison.

**Verified:** `deno test` passes (3/3 tests).


